  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Consider the following piecewise-defined function.\n$$f(x)=\\begin{cases}c(x-2)^2,&x<0\\\\ax+4,&0\\leq x\\leq2\\\\bx-4,&x>2\\end{cases}$$\nFind the values of $a$, $b$ and $c$ if $f(3)=5$, $f(1)=3$ and $f(-2)=8$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-1$, $b=3$, $c=\\frac12$.",
      "worked": "Since $3>2$, use $bx-4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3b-4&=5\\\\3b&=9\\\\b&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $0\\leq1\\leq2$, use $ax+4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a(1)+4&=3\\\\a&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-2<0$, use $c(x-2)^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}c(-2-2)^2&=8\\\\16c&=8\\\\c&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 37
  },
